SUMMARY:[Data Mining & Data Science][Machine Learning] KDD 2027 - Abstract 
 submission deadline (estimated)
DESCRIPTION:Conference title: ACM SIGKDD Conference on Knowledge Discovery 
 and Data Mining\nWebsite: https://kdd2027.kdd.org/\nSource URL: https://k
 dd2026.kdd.org/research-track-call-for-papers/\nLocation: San Jose\, Cali
 fornia\, USA\nTopics: Data Mining & Data Science\, Machine Learning\, Tim
 e Series & Sequential Data\, Federated & Distributed Learning\nSize: XL\n
 Submission type: Paper-based / mixed tracks\nConfidence: estimated\nLast 
 checked date: 2026-10-28\nNotes: Official site confirms San Jose McEnery 
 Convention Center\, Aug 1-5. Cycle 1 closed July 2026 (notification Nov 1
 4\, 2026). As of 2026-10-28 the CFP/FAQ still give no Feb 2027 Cycle 2 da
 tes\; the FAQ says it accepts new submissions. The abstract/paper dates h
 ere are AoE proxies from 2026 Cycle 2.\nScope: Knowledge discovery and da
 ta science\, centered on extracting useful structure from large\, heterog
 eneous data. Characteristic areas include clustering\, structured and rel
 ational learning\, graph and text mining\, recommender systems\, scalable
  data analysis\, and responsible data use. Generative AI is relevant when
  it advances data science\, not simply because a paper uses an LLM.\nAddi
 tional topics: Deep Representation Learning\, Natural Language Processing
  & LLMs\, Explainability & Interpretability\, Privacy-preserving ML\, ML 
 Systems & Infrastructure\nScope sources (2027): https://kdd2027.kdd.org/r
 esearch-track-call-for-papers/\nScope last checked: 2026-10-07
URL:https://kdd2026.kdd.org/research-track-call-for-papers/
